mb88: Fujitsu MB88xx 4-bit MCU core (MB8841/8843 family): mb88_core.sv and the mb88.sv wrapper.

NOT AN OPEN-SOURCE LICENSE.
These files are a SystemVerilog conversion of Dar's mb88.vhd (darfpga@aol.fr, http://darfpga.blogspot.fr; v0.3,
28/02/2017), merging the Galaga, Bosconian and Xevious copies, with many fixes by Rodimus. Dar's terms, verbatim:

    Educational use only
    Do not redistribute synthetized file with roms
    Do not redistribute roms whatever the form
    Use at your own risk

These are not open-source terms. The Rodimus changes are distributed under the same terms: Rodimus cannot grant
BSD (or any other license) over a derivative of Dar's work, and "educational use only" arguably excludes a public
repository of general-use RTL.

UNDECIDED: the author is still deciding between (a) asking Dar for a standard license in writing, (b) publishing with
Dar's terms verbatim, or (c) leaving mb88 out / rewriting it clean-room from MAME mb88xx.cpp. Do not rely on this folder
for any use beyond the terms above until that is settled. (The mb88_core.sv header once said "Greenfield"; the README
and mb88.sv say conversion, and the audit could not tell which is true from the files.)

MAME's src/devices/cpu/mb88xx/mb88xx.cpp (Ernesto Corvi, BSD-3-Clause) was used as the behavioural oracle (behaviour
checked against it, not copied):

    license: BSD-3-Clause, copyright-holders: Ernesto Corvi (MAME's header gives no year)

